## [:< ##

# name  = user-edit.form.quit
# descr = leave the interactive form, restoring the terminal first

## every exit path from the form funnels through here so terminal restore can
## never be skipped.  base.exit also fires the registered end_code callback,
## which calls user-edit.term_restore again — that is deliberate
## belt-and-braces for the paths that never reach this module [ SIGTERM ], and
## term_restore is idempotent [ it clears orig_termios on success ]

<[user-edit.term_restore]>;

<[base.exit]>;

return TRUE;

